  "solution": {
    "text": "Bond length $\\alpha \\frac{1}{\\text { bond order }}$\nBond order $=\\frac{\\text { no..of bonding } \\overline{\\mathrm{e}}-\\text { no.of antibonding } \\overline{\\mathrm{e}}}{2}$\nBond orders of $\\mathrm{O}_2^{+}, \\mathrm{O}_2^{-}, \\mathrm{O}_2^{-2}$ and $\\mathrm{O}_2^{+2}$ are respectively $2.5,1.5,1$ and 3 .",
